# oracle: third_order regular, group subset (atoms 2 5 7 of the 8-atom perturbed LJ cell), delta 1e-2, output file with the group-index and atom-ID labels
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo none, atoms 3.4e-16 (absolute).
# The file agrees with the native text byte for byte (81 entries). The third index of a line is groupmap[k]+1 in native (writeMatrix indexes groupmap by atom ID), so it is 0 for atoms outside the group: kept.
# oracle-files: w241to_lj_group.dat
# oracle-compare: thermo=none atoms=all filerel=1e-6
units           lj
atom_style      atomic
atom_modify    map array
lattice         none 1.0
region          box block 0 4 0 4 0 4
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 single 0.10 0.05 0.02 units box
create_atoms    1 single 2.05 0.12 0.08 units box
create_atoms    1 single 0.07 2.11 0.15 units box
create_atoms    1 single 2.02 2.06 0.11 units box
create_atoms    1 single 0.13 0.09 2.07 units box
create_atoms    1 single 2.09 0.04 2.13 units box
create_atoms    1 single 0.06 2.14 2.04 units box
create_atoms    1 single 2.11 2.09 2.10 units box
mass            1 1.0
pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0
neighbor        0.3 bin
group           sub id 2 5 7
third_order     sub regular 0.01 file w241to_lj_group.dat
